{"created": "2026-09-14T14:43:06.974698+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-14T14:43:07.693554+00:00", "id": 22752862, "conceptrecid": "22752861", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22752862", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22752861", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22752862", "metadata": {"title": "Bounded-index nilpotent subgroups of rational linear groups with finitely many automorphism orbits", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22752862", "publication_date": "2026-09-14", "description": "<p>Let \\(G\\leq\\operatorname{GL}_n(\\mathbb Q)\\) have finitely many orbits under its full abstract automorphism group, and put \\(d=\\dim_{\\mathbb Q}\\operatorname{span}_{\\mathbb Q}G\\). We prove that \\(G\\) has a torsion-free normal subgroup \\(U\\) satisfying \\[ \\gamma_n(U)=1,\\qquad [G:U]\\leq(2n+1)^d\\leq(2n+1)^{n^2}. \\] Thus \\(G\\) is virtually nilpotent, answering Kourovka Problem 21.40 affirmatively. More generally, if the trace set \\(T=\\{\\operatorname{tr}(g):g\\in G\\}\\) is finite, the same subgroup satisfies \\([G:U]\\leq |T|^d\\). The proof combines bounded-degree roots of algebraic numbers with the trace radical of the rational matrix algebra generated by \\(G\\). Restriction of scalars gives corresponding bounds over number fields.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Jayadevan, Achyuth", "affiliation": "Manipal Institute of Technology, MAHE", "orcid": "0009-0008-8745-4078"}], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Achxy/kourovka-llm-langgraph-benchmarks", "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22752861"}}]}}, "title": "Bounded-index nilpotent subgroups of rational linear groups with finitely many automorphism orbits", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org